      "heading": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test",
      "content": {
        "kind": "items",
        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Alternatives to an MBA include building a specialised skill, moving into a new role inside your company, taking a targeted diploma, starting a small venture or choosing a different postgraduate degree, and the right one depends on what the MBA was supposed to give you."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Name the outcome you want from an MBA, such as a role change, network or promotion, then test cheaper routes to that outcome before committing large fees."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Verify outcomes with alumni and never rely on a guaranteed salary promise."
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "proof",
      "title": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test"
